<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's 11-month oil products exports up 29 pct.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's 11-month oil products exports up 29 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's oil products exports grew 29 percent to 145.1 million barrels in the first 11 months of 1996 against 112.8 million barrels a year earlier, the Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy said on Monday.</p>
<p>The ministry said in a statement growth in oil products production and slowdown in domestic demand were behind the rise.</p>
<p>The nation's imports rose 6.3 percent to 209.4 million barrels in the first 11 months from 196.9 million a year earlier. The ministry did not give a breakdown of each product.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
